1ev6|n|One who admonishes; one who warns of faults, informs of duty, or gives advice and instruction by way of reproof or caution. ; Hence, specifically, a pupil selected to look to the school in the absence of the instructor, to notice the absence or faults of the scholars, or to instruct a division or class. ; Any large Old World lizard of the genus Varanus; esp., the Egyptian species (V. Niloticus), which is useful because it devours the eggs and young of the crocodile. It is sometimes five or six feet long. ; An ironclad war vessel, very low in the water, and having one or more heavily-armored revolving turrets, carrying heavy guns. ; A tool holder, as for a lathe, shaped like a low turret, and capable of being revolved on a vertical pivot so as to bring successively the several tools in holds into proper position for cutting.	a:1zx9,61,7;13tf,57,2;syl,54,38;og7,41,3;1z8i,39,4;l2s,37,4;1aik,34,5;8b0,34,3;1z8e,27,17;1ejx,22,4;2gkf,18,4~syl,54,38;1z8e,27,17;1zx9,61,7;1aik,34,5;1z8i,39,4;1ejx,22,4;2gkf,18,4;l2s,37,4;og7,41,3;8b0,34,3;13tf,57,2	v:765,59,69;2a5k,58,9;26d7,5,3~765,59,69;2a5k,58,9;26d7,5,3	V:2fr3,55,3;2a5k,52,6;13xi,37,2;2gji,25,1;20pj,19,4;2h15,8,4~2a5k,52,6;20pj,19,4;2h15,8,4;2fr3,55,3;13xi,37,2;2gji,25,1	n:2esf,92,6;100g,78,13;6fw,66,5;1je1,63,54;jm8,61,11;13tf,47,1;2dw6,43,9;htc,42,4;1lxf,38,13;19d0,35,3;1aik,34,5;zr,32,3;1yxc,31,17;l2s,27,2;1tnj,26,4~1je1,63,54;1yxc,31,17;2784,18,13;100g,78,13;1lxf,38,13;jm8,61,11;jdw,5,10;2dw6,43,9;ld4,6,7;1gsi,14,7;2esf,92,6;1r1j,12,6;fnv,10,5;1aik,34,5;1pxa,17,5	N:2gji,71,24;290l,55,16;o1z,48,1;htc,42,4;1el8,41,23;2e4i,37,3;17yf,36,7;zr,32,3;29qm,25,4;4bp,23,31;203f,23,2;1agg,20,3;1yxc,20,8;1gsi,14,7;1pxa,9,3~4bp,23,31;2gji,71,24;1el8,41,23;290l,55,16;jdw,8,12;1yxc,20,8;4jf,9,7;17yf,36,7;1gsi,14,7;29qm,25,4;htc,42,4;2a6g,8,3;2e4i,37,3;1agg,20,3;s56,8,3
