1f35|n|Something which stands, or remains, to keep in remembrance what is past; a memorial. ; A building, pillar, stone, or the like, erected to preserve the remembrance of a person, event, action, etc.; as, the Washington monument; the Bunker Hill monument. Also, a tomb, with memorial inscriptions. ; A stone or other permanent object, serving to indicate a limit or to mark a boundary. ; A saying, deed, or example, worthy of record.	N:2e4y,161,4~2e4y,161,4
