1fci|n|A female parent; especially, one of the human race; a woman who has borne a child. ; That which has produced or nurtured anything; source of birth or origin; generatrix. ; An old woman or matron. ; The female superior or head of a religious house, as an abbess, etc. ; Hysterical passion; hysteria. ; A film or membrane which is developed on the surface of fermented alcoholic liquids, such as vinegar, wine, etc., and acts as a means of conveying the oxygen of the air to the alcohol and other combustible principles of the liquid, thus leading to their oxidation.	a:2164,29,6;1gv5,4,4;1xvf,0,4~2164,29,6;1xvf,0,4;1gv5,4,4	V:lr2,84,9;29pe,66,1;7cd,55,5;1lms,53,6;5tk,32,2;2dwj,7,4~lr2,84,9;1lms,53,6;7cd,55,5;2dwj,7,4;5tk,32,2;29pe,66,1	N:29pe,128,76;20iy,64,2;934,47,9;1dac,46,4;18tz,43,15;5tk,32,2~29pe,128,76;18tz,43,15;934,47,9;1dac,46,4;20iy,64,2;5tk,32,2
